<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">5th Dalai Lama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1617">1617</a>–<a href="/years/1682">1682</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Fifth Dalai Lama, Ngawang Lobsang Gyatso, Great Fifth</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 5th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalai-lama">Dalai Lama</a>, Ngawang Lobsang Gyatso, was the first Dalai Lama to hold political power over all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>. In 1642 his patron <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gushi-khan">Güshi Khan</a> of the Khoshut <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> defeated the Tsangpa kings and handed him authority, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganden-monastery">Ganden</a> Phodrang government. Known as the Great Fifth, he began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potala-palace">Potala Palace</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a>, strengthened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelug">Gelug</a> school and visited the Qing court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> in 1652–1653.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/5th-dalai-lama.jpg" alt="5th Dalai Lama" width="320" height="520" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thangka_of_the_5th_Dalai_Lama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
